# What ships in the .vsix, beyond vsce's own always-excluded defaults
# (.git, .vscodeignore itself, and similar). Packaging always runs with
# `--no-dependencies` (see package.json's `package` script): this
# package's own runtime dependencies are fully satisfied without vsce's
# built-in dependency walk — @rewrap-plus/engine bundles directly into
# dist/extension.js, and web-tree-sitter loads via a runtime-computed
# path from dist/web-tree-sitter-runtime/ (src/web-tree-sitter-runtime.ts)
# — and that walk is actively harmful here: it shells out to `npm list
# --production`, which in this npm-workspaces monorepo reports the
# *workspace root* as a "dependency directory" too, so vsce tries to
# glob-and-package the entire repository (confirmed directly: `vsce ls`
# without `--no-dependencies` listed `../../.git/**` and every unrelated
# doc in the repo).

# TypeScript sources — dist/extension.js is what ships.
src/**

# Test sources and their compiled/downloaded artifacts. None of this is
# needed at runtime; the integration suite in particular pulls down a
# real VSCode build into .vscode-test/ that must never end up in a .vsix.
test/**
out-test/**
.vscode-test/**

# The build script itself — its job is done once dist/ and grammars/
# exist; it has no reason to ship.
scripts/**

# Build/type-check configuration and incremental-build caches.
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.test.json
*.tsbuildinfo
vitest.config.mts

# Source maps — useful for local debugging, not for the packaged
# extension; dropping them keeps the .vsix meaningfully smaller. Covers
# both dist/extension.js.map and dist/web-tree-sitter-runtime/*.map.
dist/**/*.map
